{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"432326df9789914e","type":"text","text":"***`Device`***\n\nDispara una alarma","x":-1185,"y":-280,"width":160,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b0debc368f8fc10b","type":"text","text":">[!success] ***`Persistencia de datos`***\n\n>***Colecciones involucradas***\n\n***`Legacy - events {isAlarm:True}`***\n***`nuevos - alarm12830`***","x":-1260,"y":-120,"width":310,"height":182,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"077f424588c4bfb8","type":"text","text":"***`client`***\n Hace un `ACK` manual de alarma recibida pulsando un botón en el cliente y enviando la petición a la API","x":-950,"y":-300,"width":280,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4dae9c370922ddec","type":"text","text":"***`API`***\n***`/api/alarm/:id/ack` ***\n","x":-580,"y":-280,"width":200,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3b4d592cf380be08","type":"text","text":">[!example] ***`Como se que es un dispositivo nuevo/viejo`***\n\n>Dependiendo del tipo de dispositivo estará en una colección u otra\n\n","x":-1280,"y":120,"width":330,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"2eb726c12856b793","type":"text","text":">[!warning] ***`Topic`***\n\n***`12830.alarm.ack`***","x":-180,"y":-188,"width":230,"height":105,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ca2a02fe3adb488b","type":"text","text":">[!warning] ***`Topic`***\n\n***`event.ack`***","x":-200,"y":-413,"width":200,"height":105,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0164d6a655e63044","type":"text","text":">***`events.stateController`***\n\n","x":50,"y":-385,"width":260,"height":50,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"7177e595c0486263","type":"text","text":"***`API`***\n- Busca en `events/alarms` por su `_id`\n\t- De no ser una alarma sale\n- Busca en `eventacks` creados con anterioridad por el _id del  evento.\n\t- si existe es que ya se izo ese `ACK` y sale\n- Se crean datos para enviar al `rabbit` con el método ***`sendEventRPC`*** dependiendo el topic manda a un micro u otro\n- Se crea un documento en la colección de ***`EventAcks`***","x":-685,"y":-62,"width":405,"height":302,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"66fd9f0097471b06","type":"text","text":">[!warning] ***`Topic`***\n\n***`event.ack.success\"`***","x":360,"y":-413,"width":200,"height":105,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"3ec5dd8a10f17ea5","type":"text","text":">***`event.notifier`***\n\n","x":600,"y":-385,"width":240,"height":50,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"7299a098eaf0a64e","type":"text","text":"***`events.stateController`***\n- Comprueba si en el `Device` existe la alarma que llego al micro como mensaje en el `topic` esta no esta seteáda como `null`\n- Asigna la información de (`ack`) a la alarma específica del dispositivo \n\n```json\n\"alarms\": {\n  \"alarm_door_open\": {\n    \"code\": \"alarm_door_open\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"startedAt\": \"2026-04-27T10:00:00.000Z\",\n    //La info que me llego del TOPIC\n    \"ack\": {\n      \"ackAt\": \"2026-04-27T10:05:00.000Z\",\n      \"ackAtGMT\": \"2026-04-27T08:05:00.000Z\",\n      \"ackBy\": \"usuario@email.com\",\n      \"comment\": \"Revisado\"\n```\n\n- Recalcula `device.noAckAlarmCount`: cuenta cuántas alarmas activas (`!== null`) tienen prioridad válida (`!== \"unassigned\"`) y todavía no tienen `ack`; si no hay `lastStatus.alarms`, pone `0`","x":-195,"y":-1020,"width":750,"height":520,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"46f0cd66eb20d014","x":-864,"y":558,"width":464,"height":202,"type":"text","text":"`Device`: Para probar: DeviceDefinition "},
		{"id":"17f8eba068f4969c","type":"text","text":">***`event.notifier.12830`***\n\n","x":140,"y":-160,"width":260,"height":50,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ab3ad130f7712de9","x":-2020,"y":-197,"width":464,"height":155,"type":"text","text":">[!tip] ***`events-12830  MICRO=updater npm star`***\nmicro para mandar una alarma con los 12830\n"}
	],
